# Local environment for the data pipeline.
#
# SETUP
#   1. cp .env.example .env.local
#   2. paste your key after the "=" below, with no quotes and no spaces
#   3. npm run env:check        # confirms it loaded, never prints the value
#
# .env.local is git-ignored and must never be committed. GitHub Actions does
# NOT read this file: CI reads the repository Actions secret of the same name.
#
# Optional. openFDA works without a key at a lower rate limit; a free key
# raises it. Get one at https://open.fda.gov/apis/authentication/
OPENFDA_API_KEY=

# Every other source this pipeline uses is public and needs no credential:
#   DailyMed, RxNorm/RxNav, Drugs@FDA, NPPES,
#   CMS Part D public files, Virginia Medicaid PDL documents.
